# Raw scrape output — large (~16 MB) and regenerable via scripts/scrape.py.
# The published page uses the normalized data.json instead.
data/*.csv
data/*.db
data/scrape_state.txt

# data/scrape_meta.json is deliberately NOT ignored — it is two lines of
# provenance behind the "Last updated" line on the page.

# Resume state for the long scrapes — meaningful only alongside the (ignored)
# CSVs they track. What they imply about coverage is baked into data.json's
# meta.incomplete at build time, so the published page carries it regardless.
data/*_scrape_progress*.json*

# --daily's own within-run resumption and the weekly diff accumulator it
# feeds -- both are transient working state (round-tripped via the GitHub
# Actions cache, not git), same category as the progress files above.
data/*_daily_progress.json*
data/daily_diff_report.json

# Working output of scripts/extract_text.py — an append-only checkpoint log
# that grows as documents are processed, not something to commit while
# prototyping.
data/doc_text.jsonl

# scripts/extract_scope.py's output — derived entirely from the file above and
# regenerated in seconds, so it travels with it rather than into git. What
# eventually gets published is a column in the payload, not this.
data/scope.jsonl

# search.sqlite itself is NOT committed -- only its chunked form is
# (search.sqlite.NNN + config.json, built by scripts/chunk_search_db.py),
# since that's what the page actually serves. Keeping both would double
# ~527 MB of published data for no benefit. Regenerable from
# data/doc_text.jsonl if the chunks ever need rebuilding.
prototype-search/search.sqlite

# Python
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS
.DS_Store
